  Three separate facts come out of that one exchange.
  (a) The session authenticated with the local `manager` account and landed at `awplus>`,
      privilege 1.  That is the correct AW+ result for a login, even for a `privilege 15`
      username.
  (b) The DUT itself lists the session: `vty 0  manager  10.38.22.33  Priv 1`.  The
      Location column holds the box's eth3 address, so the DUT agrees about who connected.
  (c) `show system` returned real, current data over the telnet session.

